<title>ITALY: Italy's Bari sees Feb CPI at minus 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bari sees Feb CPI at minus 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BARI, Italy 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bari said its February consumer price index stood at minus 0.3 percent month on month and 2.0 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In January, Bari inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 2.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bari is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 5.99 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.3   (0.2)     2.0  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3  (-0.2)     0.6  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     2.1  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -2.4   (1.4)     2.5  (5.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.2   (0.0)     1.9  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (2.1)     4.6  (4.4)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.3  (-0.1)     6.4  (7.0)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1   (0.2)     1.1  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     7.8  (8.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     1.1  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2   (0.0)     0.7  (1.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
